---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <article class="interview-article">
 


    <div class="editorial-grid">
      <!-- Visual Side -->
      <div class="editorial-visual">
        <img src="https://cdn.nhcarrigan.com/profile.png" alt="Naomi Carrigan" class="hero-img" />
      </div>

      <!-- Typography & Copy Side -->
      <div class="editorial-content">
        <h1 class="headline">
          INTERVIEW<br/>
          WITH THE<br/>
          <span>VAMPIRE</span>
        </h1>
        
        
        
        <div class="intro-block">
          <p>
            Naomi Carrigan is a transfemme software engineer committed to ethical technology development with a focus on inclusivity, sustainability, and community-driven innovation. She actively works to break down barriers in tech, support marginalized voices, and ensure her technologies respect user privacy while contributing positively to society. Her projects are open-source and community-centric.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="scroll-prompt">
          <span class="prompt-text">BEGIN TRANSCRIPT</span>
          <div class="prompt-line"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Interview Q&A Section -->
    <section class="transcript-section">
      <div class="transcript-container">
        
        <div class="qa-block">
          <span class="speaker-q">Q: While you were learning to code, what made you realize “I want to do this for real”?</span>
          <p class="answer-a">
            Honestly? Nothing! I had finished the freeCodeCamp curriculum, and was still planning on going into human resources once my unemployment stipend was exhausted. I wanted to give back to freeCodeCamp because I very much believe in the mission, but I was not burning through my nest egg any faster than I had to. So I gave my time and skills instead - which ended up leading to my first job offer and my pathway into the industry. But it didn’t start to become “oh I wanna do this forever” until I was able to move in to my current home with my sister and her boyfriend. Having the ability to provide that sort of lifestyle? No way was I gonna give that up~
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="qa-block">
          <span class="speaker-q">Q: Were there any times where you doubted your path in tech and wanted to give up? If so, how did you overcome that? And at what point in time did you feel this way?</span>
          <p class="answer-a">
           Honestly? No. I got super lucky in that my ADHD brain locked the heck in on software engineering. Still got that spark to this day~
          </p>
<br/>
<p class="answer-a">
        But I do have advice! And it is probably unconventional advice. But Naomi’s secret to staying passionate about something? Be kind to yourself. Those moments where you doubt yourself? Where you think “I’m not cut out for this?” Where you wanna throw in the towel and resign yourself to a different path in life?
          </p>
<br/>
<p class="answer-a">
Those are the moments where you need to give yourself the most grace. Those are the moments where your psyche, your body, your mind, they’re all telling you that you need a vacation. People will say “oh you just gotta power through” and like… I get where they’re coming from! Naomi very much believes that the goals worth your time are the ones that you pursue most relentlessly~
</p>

<p class="answer-a">
However! All of those down moments I mentioned earlier? You gotta listen to those! Because giving yourself the space to be human, to experience life, to pursue other passions, to feel things??? That’s part of pursuing your goals! If you do not take the rest you need, eventually you’ll be forced to rest. We call that burnout, your entire core just fizzles out and you have no desire to code. And it can last far longer than your rest~
</p>
        </div>

        <div class="qa-block">
          <span class="speaker-q">Q: You place an emphasis on creating software that focuses on inclusivity and community driven-innovation, was there any particular experience you had that made you realize there was a gap in tech not being addressed? And how exactly are you addressing this problem?</span>
          <p class="answer-a">
           I knew from the beginning that, like many things, the tech industry was very much built for specific types of people. I have been cultivating healthy online communities for far longer than I have been a software engineer - I am acutely aware of the barriers some people face for traits that are entirely beyond their control. It has always been my mission to create spaces where the folks who suffer from the systems can come to thrive, to be their authentic selves, to enjoy life.
          </p>
 <p class="answer-a">
And yes, I have encountered communities and organisations alike that are not healthy spaces for marginalised groups. I fight them however I can: carving out spaces within the community for those groups, or advocating for space in a meeting for those overlooked to be heard… but I also believe that the work I do to fight for these spaces in general also impacts the tech community. :pink_heart:
</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .interview-article {
    background: var(--bg-black);
    min-height: 100vh;
    padding: 40px 4% 100px 4%;
  }

  .article-meta-bar {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-gray);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 60px;
    margin-top: 60px;
  }


  .editorial-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.2fr;
    gap: 80px;
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 60px;
  }

  .editorial-visual {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .hero-img {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-gray);
    box-shadow: 15px 15px 0px rgba(228, 30, 129, 0.15);
  }


  .editorial-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .headline {
    font-family: 'Archivo Black', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6.5rem);
    line-height: 0.85;
    letter-spacing: -3px;
     color: var(--pink-soft);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }




  .intro-block {
    padding-left: 30px;
    margin-bottom: 60px;
  }

  .intro-block p {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    text-transform: none;
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  .scroll-prompt {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  .prompt-text {
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--pink-hot);
    letter-spacing: 2px;
  }

  .prompt-line {
    height: 1px;
    flex-grow: 1;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--pink-hot) 0%, transparent 100%);
    max-width: 200px;
  }

  /* Transcript Section Styles */
  .transcript-section {
    max-width: 1000px;
    margin: 120px auto 0 auto;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-gray);
    padding-top: 80px;
  }

  .transcript-container {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 60px;
  }

  .qa-block {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.01);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-gray);
    padding: 40px;
    position: relative;
    transition: border-color 0.3s ease;
  }

  .qa-block:hover {
    border-color: var(--pink-hot);
  }

  .speaker-q {
    font-family: 'Archivo Black', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--pink-soft);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }

  .answer-a {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
    text-transform: none;
  }

  /* Responsive Stacking */
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .editorial-grid {
      gap: 40px;
    }
    .headline {
      font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .article-meta-bar {
      margin-bottom: 40px;
    }
    .section-tag {
      display: none;
    }
    .editorial-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .hero-img {
      aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    }
    .intro-block p {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }
    .qa-block {
      padding: 25px;
    }
  }
</style>
